                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.32067/2611.32067v1/main_v4.png",
                "caption": "Figure 2:Overview of LoopDVR.Given a dense recognition model, (a) Stage 1 groups the layers of the pre-trained ViT backbone based on inter-layer representation similarity and initializes each looped backbone block using the weights of its group’s terminal layer.\n(b) Transformer block parameters are shared within each group, while each layer has a Loop Adapter to preserve depth-specific transformations.\n(c) Stage 2 distills the looped ViT using a DINOv3 teacher.\n(d) Stage 3 post-trains the resulting architecture for dense recognition, combining the looped ViT, the hybrid encoder and the looped decoder.",
                "position": 355
            }
        ]
